    "expressed_frame": {
      "group": "envelope",
      "binding": "specified",
      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "high",
      "judgment": false,
      "rule": "The same, with a stricter joint rule the node states itself: 'every infill panel must be framed on all four sides by timber, and every brace must terminate in a joint at both ends. A timber that dies into a panel' is not permitted. The German post is HALF the English one and there are more of them, which `timber-panel` records as a real difference rather than a regional accent.",
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "structural",
          "status": "canonical",
          "note": "`member_status` at ontology 0.7.0 (OQ 47). Modelled as a variant rather than a parameter because a variant can be FORBIDDEN -- `status: forbidden` is how five of these fourteen kits say the member must not appear, and a parameter has no way to say that. (The reason first recorded here was that a categorical carries no unit and the checker insists a parameter has one. That is false: this corpus holds 236 categorical parameters whose unit is `none` and `check_kits.py` passes every one. Corrected 25 Aug 2026 by audit -- the modelling call stands, its stated reason did not.)"
        }
      ]
    },
