          "status": "canonical",
          "note": "Description: 'the windows are a few paired casements in the middle of a wall of clay.' No sash of any kind belongs to this construction system."
        }
      ],
      "rule": "Small paired casements set within a single infill panel (or a pair of panels), not a sash — the panel wall wants small openings and the frame grid governs where they can go (see window_grouping_rule).",
